{#
  module/Books/view/books/library-imports/create.phtml — start a new spreadsheet import.

  This page creates the import *record* only: a name, a file path, a worksheet and the
  "complete import" flag. Nothing is read from the spreadsheet here. The import is
  simulated and then run from the edit page, which is why the submit button says
  "Simulate import" and why success redirects there — and that page stays on laminas, so
  this is a Symfony page whose success takes the visitor across the bridge.

  The requirements list and the column map are untranslated in the original; the map is
  hardcoded in the controller (`getColegioMayorLibraryFieldsMap()`), which is the only
  library whose spreadsheets this has ever been used for.
#}
{% extends 'layout.html.twig' %}

{% block content %}
<h1>{{ translate('Begin new import') }}</h1>
<p>Importing a file has the following requirements:</p>
<ol>
<li>The file to import must be of format xls or xlsx.</li>
<li>Given a specified excel file and worksheet, the first row (A) must contain the column names.</li>
<li>Each line of the worksheet must contain the withinLibraryId value, as well as a title.
    The only exception is that a row with a publicationId need not have a title defined.</li>
</ol>
<p>Currently the column mappings are unconfigurable but are mapped as follows:</p>
<dl class="dl-horizontal">
{% for field, column in fields_map %}
    <dt>{{ field }}</dt>
    <dd>{{ column }}</dd>
{% endfor %}
</dl>
{{ form_open(form, self_url) }}
{{ form_row(form.get('name')) }}
{{ form_row(form.get('libraryId'), false) }}
{{ form_row(form.get('description')) }}
{{ form_row(form.get('filePath')) }}
{{ form_row(form.get('worksheet')) }}
{{ form_row(form.get('isCompleteImport')) }}
{{ form_row(form.get('security')) }}
{{ form_row(form.get('submit')) }}
{{ form_close() }}
{% endblock %}
